p.note:
: [Aur. Vict.] Epit. 10, 5, Iurgia autem sub patre venumdata;
rapinarum cupidum; unde Neronem cuncti opinantes vocantesque summam
rerum nactum graviter acceperant.

: the use of the inf. with supersedeo (= abstineo)
is first found in the historian Sisenna (ob. 67 B.c.); not in Caes. or Cic.;
frequent in Livy and later writers.
